ame":"bob-cli-78.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-78","agent_clan_generation":"20261013031456","bead_id":"bob-cli-78.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-78[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Sub-project cascade for project blocking and the project pull-in[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A blocked project's sub-projects (project notes whose `parent:` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]names it, recursively) are Blocked too: their `^prj` and every open[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]resident are `[?]` and tagged `#prj_is_blocked`. `bob task [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]reconcile` derives this and reverses it when the ancestor's reasons[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]clear. The Task Card (Ctrl+Shift+P) applies and reverses it in the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]same gesture. Every other engine reads a tagged `^prj` as an [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]inherited reason, so nothing links, recovers, or pulls in a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]cascade-blocked task. Closing a sub-project's `^prj` that leaves [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]its parent with no open work pulls the parent's `^prj` in as Next [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](§12.10 trigger (c)), both in bob capture and in Obsidian.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]subproject_cascade.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/subproject_cascade.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-78[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-78/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Sub-project cascade contract and vectors[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: rewrite §13's residence-only rule into the cascade (parent, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ancestors, inherited reasons, ^prj tag, descendant-internal targets), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add §12.10 trigger (c) and a real step 3, and add the PDS, PDG, PDC and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PP vectors plus doc pointers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile derives, tags, and reverses the cascade[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-reconcile[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-reconcile: add a shared Rust project-tree module (parent resolution,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ancestors, descendants, tag predicate) and make reconcile block, tag, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]consume, promote, cycle-check, deproject descendant targets, and recover[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sub-projects per PDS1–PDS15.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Close paths honour the tag proxy and pull in parents[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-close[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-reconcile[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-close: make capture ! and =x closes read a tagged ^prj as an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inherited reason (PDC4/PDC5), implement pull-in step 3 and trigger (c) [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with their rows, and add the close-path subtree recovery only under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]close_recovers_subprojects.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture link guard, destinations, and & refuse cascade-blocked[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]targets[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-guards[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-reconcile[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-guards: make the capture link guard, new-task destinations, and & on[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]^prj honour the tag proxy and descendant-internal targets (PDG13, PDG15,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PDG16), with ancestor prerequisite promotion.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Navigation sub-project discovery, tag proxy, and subtree [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]planner[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-model: add bob-navigation-hotkeys sub-project discovery and a pure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]top-down subtree planner, make existing project-blocking helpers treat a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tagged ^prj as still blocked, and refuse descendant targets in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Depends on stage.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task Card Depends on and Schedule apply and reverse the [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]cascade[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-gestures[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-gestures: wire the subtree pass into every Task Card Depends on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]writer and, under schedule_cascade, every ^prj Schedule writer, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]descendant writes, link consumption, commitment transfer, notices, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deploy.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cycler and block-id-prompt honour the cascade and pull in [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]parents[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler: make task-status-cycler and block-id-prompt read a tagged ^prj [/#